{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require food brands to publicise intended rebrands with notice",
        "additional_details": "For example, a change on a drink from a pull top to a different spout can result in a child refusing to drink that product. If parents of SEN kids had notice to change, we could stock pile safe foods and work on a gentle transition so our kids stay fed and have time to build trust with the new packaging.",
        "background": "When food companies change their packaging/branding, this can turn a SEN child\u2019s safe food into an unsafe food. There should be a law that states food brands have to publicise their intentions to do so maybe a month before launch. For some SEN children and parents, it\u2019s never just a packaging change",
